I wrote the session plan: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. Git refused the add rather than failing, and I didn't force it with -f. The files are on disk for the implementation phase.

Task 1: Fixes #1221 (product). With --output-format stream-json, a SIGTERM, SIGHUP or SIGQUIT still kills the process mid-stream. No closing event is written, nothing goes to stderr, and nothing says the -o file wasn't written. The task copies this morning's json fix (17450aae):
• Catch the signal for stream-json runs too.
• End the stream with one result event marked is_error: true.
• Print (interrupted) on stderr, along with the existing note that the -o file was not written.
• Exit 143/129/131 and leave the -o file untouched.

The task file orders the work:
1. Measure the current binary first and post that table on #1221 before any code changes.
2. Add tests against the existing stall stub, plus a check that they fail by name when the fix is disabled.
3. Post the after-table before the full build-and-test run.
4. Update the docs paragraph on signals.

This is the last open part of #1221. If any part of the ticket's done-when is still false at the end, the task must file it as a new issue, because the harness re-applies "Fixes #1221" to leftover commits (#1215).

Task 2: Fixes #1225 (evolve, backlog drain). If the guard that an_unclosed_quote_spawns_nothing checks ever regresses, running that test creates real worktrees and run files in the repo. The task:
• Adds a test-only check where /spawn creates worktrees and run files: under cargo test, it panics if the target is the project root instead of creating anything.
• Adds a test of the argument parser that catches the unclosed quote, so the refusal is covered without touching the filesystem.
• Requires disabling the guard as one command, with git worktree list and the run-file listing recorded before and after. They must be identical.

Both tasks warn about the file-size limit: src/prompt.rs and src/commands_spawn.rs are at or near their recorded sizes in tests/module_size.rs, and src/context.rs and src/format/mod.rs are off-limits.

